          <div class="wf-faq-answer">
            <p>Wet, matted leaves that are glued to the soil reduce pickup efficiency, so letting them dry makes a huge difference. Loose landscape mulch tends to get thrown rather than gathered. It collects loose surface thatch rather than pulling up roots, and very large pine cones are occasionally rolled over rather than scooped.</p>
